# README - Insurance App

## 🚀 Project Setup

### 1️⃣ Install Dependencies
```sh
npm install
```

### 2️⃣ Run the Application
```sh
npm start
```

### 3️⃣ Available Commands
| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `npm start` | Deletes any existing PM2 process and starts the app using PM2 |
| `npm run stop` | Stops and deletes the PM2 process |
| `npm run restart` | Restarts the PM2 process |
| `npm run logs` | Shows real-time logs for the application |
| `npm run list` | Lists all running PM2 processes |
| `npm run nodemon` | Starts the app in development mode with Nodemon |

### 4️⃣ Ensure to stop server when not using cause ir runs in background
```sh
npm run stop
```

#### 📍 Track CPU Usage & Restart if >70%
- **Process:** Uses a Node Scheduler to monitor CPU and restart the server if usage exceeds 70%.


---

## 📌 API Documentation

For full API details, check [`api-docs.md`](api-docs.md)

## 📌 Deployment Notes
- Ensure MongoDB is running (`mongodb://localhost:27017/insuranceDB`).
- PM2 must be installed globally (`npm install -g pm2`).

